-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-textshadow:undefined;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-textstroke:undefined;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-letterspacing:0px;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-texttransform:undefined"><span style="width:100%"><p>How fast will I see results?</p></span></div><div data-rid="9158030c-9331-4296-9a05-f68f7df0cb06" class="r-13xolqa"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand" style="width:var(--rsw, 100%);height:100%" class="r-1z05td0" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M8 4a.5.5 0 0 1 .5.5v3h3a.5.5 0 0 1 0 1h-3v3a.5.5 0 0 1-1 0v-3h-3a.5.5 0 0 1 0-1h3v-3A.5.5 0 0 1 8 4"></path></svg></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:R3dr2:"><div data-rid="17b30015-1a13-4286-98e0-a1b428bd7b77" class="r-fdd2ki"><div data-rid="3e23bc80-b2e5-4ddc-9cb5-b478dd7285b2" class="r-8665z7 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Most women notice improvements in energy, mood, and digestion within the first few weeks. Because hormones operate on intricate feedback loops, more significant changes, like potential ease from cramps or bloating, often require 2-3 cycles. This allows monthlies to work with your body’s natural rhythms for lasting results.</p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="4b3457ec-dca2-4b19-8d6b-3499d33c398d" class="r-e60f4x" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="5d05f148-d27e-4920-b705-44fe64a187b1" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:R5dr2:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-1at35j6"><div data-rid="75ca9fdb-e57e-4115-b2e4-3fafcd948b7d" class="r-13rrbib alchemy-rte" style="--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-color:#2A2A2A;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-fontsize:14px;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-textdecoration:undefined;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-fontfamily:Quicksand;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-fontweight:400;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-lineheight:125%;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-textshadow:undefined;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-textstroke:undefined;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-letterspacing:0px;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-texttransform:undefined"><span style="width:100%"><p>What is the HPO axis, and why is it important?</p></span></div><div data-rid="28ce2575-2247-4fd1-94b2-2678c0ca25c1" class="r-dbhhie"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand" style="width:var(--rsw, 100%);height:100%" class="r-xj3ral" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M8 4a.5.5 0 0 1 .5.5v3h3a.5.5 0 0 1 0 1h-3v3a.5.5 0 0 1-1 0v-3h-3a.5.5 0 0 1 0-1h3v-3A.5.5 0 0 1 8 4"></path></svg></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:R5dr2:"><div data-rid="411bfbec-5f4f-4330-9ce6-ec304e38997d" class="r-1egklox"><div data-rid="fbccdf67-b67f-4332-929c-aab439794a26" class="r-g66geo alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">The HPO axis stands for the Hypothalamus-Pituitary-Ovarian axis, and it’s like your body’s hormonal command centre. Here’s how it works:</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">Hypothalamus (The Coordinator): </span></strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">This part of your brain sends out signals (called GnRH) to kickstart hormone production. It’s also highly sensitive to stress, sleep, and nutrition, which can disrupt the entire process.</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">Pituitary Gland (The Messenger):</span></strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)"> The pituitary gland receives signals from the hypothalamus and produces key hormones like FSH (follicle-stimulating hormone) and LH (luteinizing hormone). These control your cycle rhythm and regulate things like water retention and sugar metabolism.</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">Ovaries (The Hormone Producers): </span></strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">Your ovaries respond to the pituitary gland’s signals by producing estrogen and progesterone. These hormones are responsible for managing symptoms like cramps, mood swings, and bloating, as well as regulating prostaglandins, which can cause pain during your period.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">When this system is in balance, your body works smoothly. But when it’s thrown off by factors like stress, nutrient gaps, or lifestyle changes, the feedback loops misfire. This can cause your body to overreact, leading to bloating, pain, mood swings, fatigue, and other cycle-related symptoms.</span></p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="44ccae00-5f11-45c0-ae59-5a5c3f4fda5f" class="r-19kw4u" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="c24a5c15-16b9-4a0a-9a03-21e639680ac8" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:R7dr2:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-1ra6ph1"><div data-rid="9324fdd2-4a9e-4026-ad03-0d9b2cb4221d" class="r-c410o8 alchemy-rte" style="--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-color:#2A2A2A;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-fontsize:14px;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-textdecoration:undefined;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-fontfamily:Quicksand;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-fontweight:400;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-lineheight:125%;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-textshadow:undefined;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-textstroke:undefined;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-letterspacing:0px;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-texttransform:undefined"><span style="width:100%"><p>When and how should I take monthlies?</p></span></div><div data-rid="6b1568af-ee4c-49f9-a6f2-05b1221897f9" class="r-a1qlht"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand" style="width:var(--rsw, 100%);height:100%" class="r-inchx9" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M8 4a.5.5 0 0 1 .5.5v3h3a.5.5 0 0 1 0 1h-3v3a.5.5 0 0 1-1 0v-3h-3a.5.5 0 0 1 0-1h3v-3A.5.5 0 0 1 8 4"></path></svg></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:R7dr2:"><div data-rid="75a70dea-a1df-4fe6-a78b-72f1e2c920d0" class="r-pdfkyu"><div data-rid="c67e04ff-3cd2-4eb6-a1b8-d16bce915284" class="r-j3sqc9 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Take monthlies once daily in the morning with food. Simply mix one scoop with water or your favourite beverage. Consistent use is essential to experience the full benefits, as it works with your body’s natural cycles.*</p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="53398187-a2c1-4b83-8ef3-947c1639a799" class="r-qjjjkd" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="f55deefc-9973-4a6b-bae5-5c8abcc0a960" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:R9dr2:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-4oixzj"><div data-rid="8f115d26-b24b-4002-8dc8-054a10eec640" class="r-1sdie3e alchemy-rte" style="--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-color:#2A2A2A;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-fontsize:14px;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-textdecoration:undefined;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-fontfamily:Quicksand;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-fontweight:400;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-lineheight:125%;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-textshadow:undefined;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-textstroke:undefined;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-letterspacing:0px;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a