<br><span style="font-weight: normal;"><br>1. Results may vary based on individual factors such as starting health, lifestyle, adherence to recommendations, and other unique circumstances.<br><br>2. Proper diet, exercise, and hydration are essential for achieving and maintaining health benefits.<br><br>3. If you are pregnant, breastfeeding, taking medications, or have an existing medical condition, consult your healthcare provider before using monthlies or any other supplements.</span><br><br><br>Study References:<br><br><span style="font-weight: normal;">The impact of menstrual symptoms on everyday life: a survey among 42,879 women Harlow, S. D., & Park, M. (1996). American Journal of Obstetrics and Gynecology, 174(2), 683-689. https://www.ajog.org/article/S0002-9378(19)30427-2/abstract<br></span><br><span style="font-weight: normal;">NSAID Resistance in Dysmenorrhea: Epidemiology, Causes, and Treatment Options
